SELECT 'artist_biography', 'en', 1, '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"El Blachy —born Blas Darío Fragoso in Santo Domingo in 1981 and raised in Santiago de los Caballeros— is a Dominican merengue típico singer and songwriter who became one of the genre’s leading names in the 2020s, winning the Premios Soberano for Conjunto Típico in 2024 and 2025.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Years in the big orchestras","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"He began in the «Merengue Band», the house orchestra of the «Hotel Jaragua», where he stayed a year, then spent five years in the orchestra of ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"2bc36959-dcce-4e10-9ecf-2cd418eaa489","displayText":"Wilfrido Vargas","occurrenceId":"0d18731e-68e1-41df-96b0-b23026e0202e"}},{"text":" and nine with ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"76c3c113-eea0-4dbd-8e71-c7dc6662c86c","displayText":"Yovanny Polanco","occurrenceId":"04d87c3a-6c6f-4c46-9d74-bf2e3dcc9dce"}},{"text":", whom he later described as being like a father to him. He also passed through ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"d133f2df-cb21-4dd4-8673-8efb63e6cc5d","displayText":"Banda Real","occurrenceId":"3805b745-2c2c-419a-bcd4-d5f71f3051db"}},{"text":", which he calls his “university” and where he recorded «Perdido sin ti», a song he also wrote. His nickname comes from his grandfather, who was known by the same name.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"A solo project","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"76c3c113-eea0-4dbd-8e71-c7dc6662c86c","displayText":"Yovanny Polanco","occurrenceId":"9e2fed47-6035-4d10-9c26-39edfbea6856"}},{"text":" announced a break from the stage shortly before the pandemic, El Blachy struck out on his own. After a 2020 ballad-crossover tour, «En Romantiqueo Tours», he presented his own típico group in December 2020, «El Blachy y su Romantiqueo Típico», debuting with a típico cover of «La Nochecita», a song by Lenier and El Micha with Jacob Forever, arranged by Israel Almonte.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"«Hola perdida» and the Soberano","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"His breakthrough came with a merengue típico version of «Hola perdida», a song by the Argentine artist Luck Ra, after an earlier single, «A qué vuelves», went largely unnoticed. He also turned Maluma’s «Sobrio» into típico, and recorded «Pa’ Perderte» with ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"358ff3da-d3b2-4158-b601-3abc1005f927","displayText":"Manny Cruz","occurrenceId":"a5bce6bd-1939-443e-8e9b-a19829fccb2f"}},{"text":". At the March 2024 Premios Soberano he won Conjunto Típico, reported at the time as beating ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"76c3c113-eea0-4dbd-8e71-c7dc6662c86c","displayText":"Yovanny Polanco","occurrenceId":"fb89ac17-1414-4e7e-925e-119603d4d78b"}},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"15c08a48-b94b-41c8-99d8-53144397c787","displayText":"Krisspy","occurrenceId":"c264faad-b7b4-4404-ad3c-68a489726249"}},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"d133f2df-cb21-4dd4-8673-8efb63e6cc5d","displayText":"Banda Real","occurrenceId":"4e9f2bc2-c691-480b-9856-0d3b9287fbb5"}},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"f07fcc6b-a888-4e97-ac50-6ce6ea37a714","displayText":"El Prodigio","occurrenceId":"6a0c589f-334f-4fed-8aa0-f9629b22ea05"}},{"text":"; he won the category again in 2025. He has said he keeps his lyrics clean because children are among his listeners.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Legacy","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"By late 2024 El Blachy was booking around forty parties in November and sixty in December, and had announced collaborations with ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"cf438c62-e0b8-4ba9-8e4b-f328ddce0c9b","displayText":"Chimbala","occurrenceId":"dde104ae-bb94-4701-a7e2-8e736e393344"}},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"550df3b5-6488-4aec-a476-a5d28d52ceea","displayText":"Bulin 47","occurrenceId":"e8b6025a-2f28-4022-882f-28ea7636fb0e"}},{"text":". In August 2026 he filled the Coca-Cola Music Hall in Puerto Rico, part of a run of international dates that includes a tour of the United States.","type":"text"}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', id, 1 FROM artists WHERE slug = 'el-blachy'
